{{SQLExecution.withNewExecutionId0}} can throw {{NumberFormatException: Cannot parse null string}} at the line:
{code:scala}
val rootExecutionId = sc.getLocalProperty(EXECUTION_ROOT_ID_KEY).toLong
{code}

The current code checks if {{EXECUTION_ROOT_ID_KEY}} is null, sets it if so, then *re-reads* it from local properties assuming it is non-null:
{code:scala}
if (sc.getLocalProperty(EXECUTION_ROOT_ID_KEY) == null) {
  sc.setLocalProperty(EXECUTION_ROOT_ID_KEY, executionId.toString)
  sc.addJobTag(executionIdJobTag(sparkSession, executionId))
}
val rootExecutionId = sc.getLocalProperty(EXECUTION_ROOT_ID_KEY).toLong // crashes here
{code}

This re-read can return null under high-concurrency scenarios involving nested thread pools (e.g., {{CrossValidator(parallelism=4)}} with {{OneVsRest(parallelism=2)}} running from a Python {{ThreadPoolExecutor}}).

The fix is to read the property once and use the value directly, avoiding the re-read:
{code:scala}
val existingRootId = sc.getLocalProperty(EXECUTION_ROOT_ID_KEY)
val rootExecutionId = if (existingRootId != null) {
  existingRootId.toLong
} else {
  sc.setLocalProperty(EXECUTION_ROOT_ID_KEY, executionId.toString)
  sc.addJobTag(executionIdJobTag(sparkSession, executionId))
  executionId
}
{code}

